# RCRM iOS project rules

- Native iOS 17+ app using Swift 5.9+ and SwiftUI. Use FirebaseCore, FirebaseAuth and FirebaseFirestore; do not add third-party UI libraries.
- Use the Space-Glass & Neon Dark design system: dark space gradients, frosted panels, cyan/purple/green/pink/blue neon accents and legible light text. Reuse the shared theme components.
- Keep Swift sources in the app target and build complete, compilable code without placeholders.
- Android is the schema authority. Firestore `leads/{leadId}` stores `ownerId`, `name`, `phone`, `email`, `address`, `company`, `jobTitle`, `notes`, comma-separated `category` and `targetMarket`, `salesStage`, `recruitStage`, `followUpDate`, `isPaused`, `isClosed`, `pausedReason`, `lastAttemptedContact`, and `lastConnectedContact`; it can contain other Android fields. Preserve unedited fields. The `tmMarried`, `tmAge`, `tmChildren`, `tmHomeowner`, and `tmOccupation` booleans mirror `targetMarket` for iOS.
- `leads/{leadId}/next_actions/{actionId}` contains `ownerId`, `leadId`, `workflow`, `type`, `title`, `notes`, `dueTime`, `status`, and optional appointment/completion metadata. `leads/{leadId}/activity_records/{recordId}` contains `ownerId`, `leadId`, `type`, `outcome`, `note`, and `timestamp`. `user_settings/{uid}` includes `role`, `email`, `managed_users`, settings, and `daily_stats/{day}`.
- Every leads query must filter `ownerId` to the authenticated user ID. Every lead create or update must set `ownerId` to that ID. Child writes must include the authenticated `ownerId` and parent `leadId`; follow Android Firestore rules. Deleting a lead does not delete its subcollections automatically.
- Date fields may be Firestore timestamps or epoch milliseconds; preserve Android-compatible formats. Sales stages: `new_lead`, `contacted`, `appt_set`, `presentation`, `app_submitted`, `in_force`. Recruit stages: `prospect`, `invited_bop`, `interviewed`, `iba_submitted`, `licensing`, `licensed_active`. Action types: `CALL`, `MESSAGE`, `MEETING`, `TO_DO`, `EMAIL`. Action statuses: `PENDING`, `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `PAUSED`.
